Issue #25 is still open: the fix is committed but not landed on main. It is queued with the manager again, and I've marked the issue `Blocked-by: tacplus-dev/looper#113`.

- **Fix (`b998d87`, on main `24bbb18`):**
  - The `Dockerfile` creates a system user and group `llmproxy` with the fixed UID/GID 65532 and sets `USER 65532:65532` before the `ENTRYPOINT`. llmproxy writes nothing to disk, so no directory needed to change owner.
  - `just gates` now also runs `just image-user`, which fails unless the Dockerfile's last `USER` is `65532:65532`.
  - STATE.md is updated. PROPOSALS.md suggests the operator set `runAsUser`/`runAsGroup` 65532 on llmproxy's pods; that change belongs in tacplus-dev/operator.
- **Checks I ran here:**
  - semgrep 1.183.0 with `p/default` reports 0 findings on the Dockerfile; before the fix it reported `missing-user-entrypoint`.
  - `just image-user` passes.
  - `looper-trace check` passes. It found no handlers, and the change touches none.
- **Not verified:** that the image still starts, which is one of the issue's two done-when items. There's no container runtime here, and no build job has finished yet.
- **Lands:** five attempts so far, none failed because of the change. Three hit "no verdict within 3h", one got a GitLab 422 and never started, and today's attempt was killed mid-build (exit 143). Those are the build-infrastructure failures tracked in tacplus-dev/looper#113, which also hold up gateway#29 and opa#9. I re-queued the land at 12:59Z, and the manager will post its verdict on the issue.
- **Backport:** PR #26 against release/0.1 is open and mergeable, and its description names the tag to cut once it merges, `v0.1.7`. No patch tag goes on main, because main has carried #13 since `v0.1.3` and that belongs to the next minor release.

I posted this status on the issue and wrote the `Blocked-by` line to the run's outcome file, which ends this run. Once the fix lands, the next run posts the outcome comment and closes the issue.
